+  gts_astral_rift.2705.desc: "Breaking through the churning clouds, we saw a sky even blacker than the misty ground below. The sky is a boundless curtain with a more regular and fine vertical and horizontal arrangement than the ground - undoubtedly, it is a giant net!\n\nEven more incredible is that this giant net is regularly expanding and contracting on an immeasurable scale. As we continued to try to get closer, we realized that behind this net was a giant wall, whose vertical movement was even more exaggerated.\n\nWind constantly swept past our hull, and as we approached the range of the giant wall's undulations, every gust became more violent.\n\nThe strong signal from the biological sensors confirmed our conjecture - §YWe are on the sole of a Giantess!§!\n\nEven more wonderful is that another weak biological signal around us seems to change regularly with the airflow in the wind. These airflows are not just a special weather pattern; their behavior is also unusually precise. More importantly, we discovered a hormone-like compound in the swirling air. Subsequent analysis showed that this is surprisingly similar to the biological reaction of plants when attacked."
