   # Original: 足垢洞穴
   gts_astral_rift.2710.name: "Foot Grime Cave"
-  # Original: 我们顺着无情的狂风深入周围的山谷，穿过厚厚的含硫孢子云，越是深入，岩壁的颜色愈发趋近黄褐，岩壁的构成似乎正发生变化，这同样体现在更加狭窄的谷隙上。\n\n钻入谷壁上的某处罅隙之后，我们进入了一个豁然开朗的洞窟。厚厚的钟乳石把浑浊的液体滴在黄疸的土壤上，土壤里充满了黄色的真菌。在一簇簇蘑菇之间，成群的昆虫在潮湿的地面上轻快地飞舞，昏暗处生长着苍白的植被。陡峭的墙壁上长满了苔藓，浑浊的空气中弥漫着一层厚厚的孢子雾。\n\n此处的生态环境如此特殊，让[this.GetName]联想到了此前寄居于她足下的某个真菌类物种。对黄褐岩石的详细分析证实了这个猜想——§Y我们正在另一个尺寸难以计量的巨娘足下！§!\n\n更确切地说，是她的鞋垫足垢之中的某处角落，与那些寄居在我们足下的卑微物种相同！\n\n此外，在洞里，我们探测到一个微弱的电场：一个由冲动和突触组成的网络，它似乎连接着各种真菌群。也许我们可以进入这个网络，与这些巨娘足下的原生真菌物种深入交流。
-  gts_astral_rift.2710.desc: "We followed the ruthless gale deep into the surrounding valleys, passing through thick clouds of sulfurous spores. The deeper we went, the more the color of the rock walls approached yellow-brown, and the composition of the rock walls seemed to be changing, which was also reflected in the narrower valley gaps.\n\nAfter drilling into a crevice on the valley wall, we entered a cave that suddenly opened up. Thick stalactites dripped turbid liquid onto the jaundiced soil, which was filled with yellow fungi. Between clusters of mushrooms, swarms of insects flew briskly on the damp ground, and pale vegetation grew in the dimness. The steep walls were covered with moss, and the murky air was filled with a thick layer of spore mist.\n\nThe ecological environment here is so special that it reminded [this.GetName] of a certain fungal species that previously lived under her feet. Detailed analysis of the yellow-brown rocks confirmed this conjecture—§YWe are under the foot of another Giantess of immeasurable size!§!\n\nMore precisely, in some corner of the grime on her shoe insole, identical to those humble species living under our feet!\n\nIn addition, inside the cave, we detected a weak electric field: a network composed of impulses and synapses, which seems to connect various fungal colonies. Perhaps we can access this network and communicate deeply with these native fungi under the Giantess's foot."
+  # Original: 我们顺着无情的狂风深入周围的山谷，穿过厚厚的含硫孢子云，越是深入，岩壁的颜色愈发趋近黄褐，岩壁的构成似乎正发生变化，这同样体现在更加狭窄的谷隙上。\n\n钻入谷壁上的某处罅隙之后，我们进入了一个豁然开朗的洞窟。厚厚的钟乳石把浑浊的液体滴在黄疸的土壤上，土壤里充满了黄色的真菌。在一簇簇蘑菇之间，成群的昆虫在潮湿的地面上轻快地飞舞，昏暗处生长着苍白的植被。陡峭的墙壁上长满了苔藓，浑浊的空气中弥漫着一层厚厚的孢子雾。\n\n此处的生态环境如此特殊，让[this.GetName]联想到了此前寄居于她足下的某个真菌类物种。对黄褐岩石的详细分析证实了这个猜想 -  - §Y我们正在另一个尺寸难以计量的巨娘足下！§!\n\n更确切地说，是她的鞋垫足垢之中的某处角落，与那些寄居在我们足下的卑微物种相同！\n\n此外，在洞里，我们探测到一个微弱的电场：一个由冲动和突触组成的网络，它似乎连接着各种真菌群。也许我们可以进入这个网络，与这些巨娘足下的原生真菌物种深入交流。
+  gts_astral_rift.2710.desc: "We followed the ruthless gale deep into the surrounding valleys, passing through thick clouds of sulfurous spores. The deeper we went, the more the color of the rock walls approached yellow-brown, and the composition of the rock walls seemed to be changing, which was also reflected in the narrower valley gaps.\n\nAfter drilling into a crevice on the valley wall, we entered a cave that suddenly opened up. Thick stalactites dripped turbid liquid onto the jaundiced soil, which was filled with yellow fungi. Between clusters of mushrooms, swarms of insects flew briskly on the damp ground, and pale vegetation grew in the dimness. The steep walls were covered with moss, and the murky air was filled with a thick layer of spore mist.\n\nThe ecological environment here is so special that it reminded [this.GetName] of a certain fungal species that previously lived under her feet. Detailed analysis of the yellow-brown rocks confirmed this conjecture - §YWe are under the foot of another Giantess of immeasurable size!§!\n\nMore precisely, in some corner of the grime on her shoe insole, identical to those humble species living under our feet!\n\nIn addition, inside the cave, we detected a weak electric field: a network composed of impulses and synapses, which seems to connect various fungal colonies. Perhaps we can access this network and communicate deeply with these native fungi under the Giantess's foot."
