   gts_astral_rift.1305.b: "Use emergency gas."
   # Original: 腔室
   gts_astral_rift.1310.name: "Chamber"
-  # Original: 沿着隧道壁的层流航行，再参照§E[event_target:gts_astral_rift_fluid.GetName]§!的生命体征数据，我们在探索过程中良好地保持在血管中心。\n\n几天过去了，没有什么大事发生。我们周围的盘状异物无疑是血红细胞。而不时掠过的血红不规则残片和半透明无定形团块，更加证实了我们正处于§E[event_target:gts_astral_rift_fluid.GetName]§!的血液中\n\n我们曾远远看到§E[event_target:gts_astral_rift_fluid.GetName]§!那“遮天蔽日”的身躯——举手投足都传递出恐怖的压迫力。\n\n毫无疑问，我们过去曾有过的一切强烈感受也难与此刻匹敌——“身处”如此巨大的少女躯体之中的震撼。\n\n我们应当庆幸，我们的存在还未被少女体内的任何自然防御系统注意到。当然，更罔论§E[event_target:gts_astral_rift_fluid.GetName]§!本人的注意了。\n\n现在，我们发现自己置身于一个巨大的腔室。壁上排列着静脉状突起。腔壁有规律地膨胀和收缩，迫使数百万升的液体通过一个出口。\n\n当我们尝试维持位置时，发现了第二个进入舱室的入口。微量的结晶物质悬浮在从隧道流出的液体中。水流的压力很低，只要用一些巧妙的导航，就可以探测到这个孔口。
-  gts_astral_rift.1310.desc.common: "Navigating along the laminar flow of the tunnel walls and referencing the vital signs data of §E[event_target:gts_astral_rift_fluid.GetName]§!, we managed to stay well within the center of the vessel during our exploration.\n\nDays passed without major incident. The disc-shaped foreign objects around us are undoubtedly red blood cells. The occasional red irregular fragments and semi-transparent amorphous masses further confirm that we are in the blood of §E[event_target:gts_astral_rift_fluid.GetName]§!\n\nWe once saw the body of §E[event_target:gts_astral_rift_fluid.GetName]§! from afar—\"blotting out the sky and sun\"—every movement conveying terrifying oppression.\n\nUndoubtedly, no intense feeling we've had in the past can rival this moment—the shock of being \"inside\" the body of such a gigantic girl.\n\nWe should be thankful that our presence has not been noticed by any natural defense systems within the girl's body. Let alone by §E[event_target:gts_astral_rift_fluid.GetName]§! herself.\n\nNow, we find ourselves in a massive chamber. The walls are lined with venous protrusions. The chamber walls expand and contract rhythmically, forcing millions of liters of fluid through an exit.\n\nAs we attempted to maintain our position, we discovered a second entrance to the chamber. Traces of crystalline substance are suspended in the fluid flowing out of the tunnel. The current pressure is low, and with some clever navigation, we can probe this orifice."
