   gts_hoppo.10.name: "Crossroads"
-  gts_hoppo.10.desc: "If that girl was in a hurry to get to our capital complex, she certainly did not show it.\n\nHer steps were slow and measured, albeit with barely contained excitement: she was clearly aware that if she decided to just start running around at random, the planet would probably not last a minute or two.\n\nOf course, this did nothing to reduce her devastation. With each kiss of her smooth soles against the crust, hundreds of thousands of square kilometers of land just…vanished. It would be impossible to tell what was ever there, and while this certainly included the works of our civilization, even the great natural structures would be gone so they would not stand a chance. The highest mountain in the world, capturing the imagination of countless for millennia, finally conquered by brave mountaineers thanks to centuries of attempts - held her bare foot for only an instant as it was compressed and melted into lava, pushed tens of kilometers into the mantle. The girl was doing nothing, merely trodding on it, and turned the highest part of the world into the deepest basin on Earth-though this wasn't so unique, there are plenty of those now on this planet.\n\nOf course, the cities didn't fare any better - and really, if the girl wasn't actively looking for them she probably wouldn't even notice stepping onto them.\n\nUnfortunately, she *did* notice. She did notice the tiny grey stains calling themselves ‘metropolises’. No matter how big they are, no matter how storied their past, no matter how many people called them home – she cared only about how to wipe them out.\n\nSome of those cities she did not dwell on. A great port city, situated amongst a coastal bay, with countless ships heading from it to send goods across the world was an important center for traffic in this vast region. And in a sudden roar and the ensuing earth tremors, the bay became much bigger - much, much bigger, the new bay shaped very much like the five toes of her foot along with its front pad.  Ships, infrastructure, vehicles that once traveled across the world, they were now moving faster than ever before – though as dust and specks stuck to her sole and moved by her footsteps.\n\nOthers, she found amusing. A cultural hub, home to some of the largest museums outside of the capital complex, its long history surviving wars and natural catastrophes with its precious memories of our civilization intact: But none of this earned the girl’s respect as she simply scratched the entire region away with her toes. Castles, palaces, ruins, monuments - the whole region became compressed into tiny mounds the size of her toes as she moved, more insignificant victims under her toenails.\n\nShe heard that this region was home to the world’s best cooking technology. That its signature dishes have travelled around the globe, through even our empire. Quality ingredients, grown carefully to achieve the best tastes, combined with a long history of culinary tradition to form wondrous meals: She simply *had* to try some, you know? She laid down, an action that instantly eradicated numerous less interesting cities and countless insignificant ‘germs’. And as she stood back up, merely brushing off the residue of an entire sub-continent off her dress and continued her travels she ultimately concluded  she could not feel the appeal of the cuisine, only leaving behind a few giant craters left by her tongue lapping onto it embedded into the crust of the planet, the craters caked in spit and the occasional scraps of civilization.\n\nAnd finally, as she reached the other side of the world -  a regional capital of forty million people, a spectacular economic hub that was crushed into nothing under her curious toes - her smile grew ever larger. She moved carefully for a few steps (carefully as in causing minimal tremors, though this made no major difference to the areas directly under her feet) now finally arriving at the capital complex. She stopped, slowly crouched to get closer. It did nothing - her face was still thousands of kilometers away in the sky.\n\nHer voice,
-    a mere whisper, shattered every window in the region, weaker buildings collapsing into plumes of dust that were immediately dispelled by the frighteningly loud sound. Even if she noticed, she did not care.\n\n\n\n§R“Hello, [Root.Leader.GetName] ! Sorry, your planet was too cute, I simply had to play with it. But, mmm…yes! I've come to offer you a deal.”§!\n\nShe became more serious, a look of concentration spreading across her face.\n\n§R“I heard that you guys invented something that can make things smaller. My sister needs it! See, she loves breaking stuff. She always tells me stories of breaking things. But now she's too big and everything is so small it barely exists. So! If you made her smaller, she can break stuff again - and she can break stuff for you that you want destroyed.”§!\n\nShe opened her arms excitedly: a small fleet of ships, completely unnoticed, on an evac mission did not even get a chance to realize what was happening as they were wiped out by the sleeve of her glove.\n\n§R“So, [Root.Leader.GetName]? Good deal, right? It’s great, right? You guys are going to love how good my big sis is at wiping out anything she wants!”§!\n\nThe advisors, shocked, confused, and borderline deaf, stared at this happy, godlike child, who after erasing almost three billion lives for fun, was asking for our help. Do we…do we want to help her? More importantly are we willing to risk ticking her off by refusing?"
