-  gts_huatian.1021.desc: "Today the morning sun is just right, a good day for baking cakes\n\nThe morning sun shines lazily through the kitchen lattice window on the tidy stove, and also on a small figure busy on the table.\n\nThat is a cute tiny person only slightly larger than half a palm. Translucent over-knee white stockings, shiny little leather shoes on feet, a standard black and white maid outfit, and further up is aqua blue long hair obediently lying on the shoulders. A pair of eyes clear as sapphires flashing with the light unique to industrious children—it is none other than the little maid of the Kurohane family, Huatian Liuye, Little Huatian.\n\nToday is a very special day. The breakfast to be prepared for the master is a delicious cake. But since it is for the master, naturally it won't be an ordinary cake. For this, Huatian got up early to prepare the batter and put it in the oven, then preparing to make the accompanying drink while the cake bakes.\n\nLittle Huatian accustomed to tiptoeing, but used magic to open the cupboard above, took out a white porcelain teacup with golden patterns and a matching spoon, then came to the other side under the cupboard window, looking at the two rows of special seasoning boxes.\n\nThis is the most luxurious seasoning in the world.\n\nHands working together to open one of the boxes, inside are full of small balls like black water babies, faintly flickering with fine yellow and purple light spots. Even using the tiny person Huatian as a reference, these small balls are only the size of basketballs—but every small ball here is a complete universe.\n\nThat's right, size is always relative. No one stipulated that the giantess little maid Little Huatian cannot simultaneously be a giantess who can easily crush the tiny universe. For Little Huatian, this is already a quite natural thing.\n\nHuatian waved her small hand, and a large number of universes flew into the teacup following the guide, stopping only when about three-quarters of the cup was filled. Then Huatian also came to the teacup, first putting the special sugar cubes held in her arms for dissolving the universe barriers into the teacup, then struggling to pick up that spoon from the table. After staggering, she finally held the spoon high above her head and put it into the teacup, pulled out a hand to wipe the nonexistent fragrant sweat on her forehead, tiptoed and hugged the spoon with both hands to stir. The barriers of the universes were instantly shattered by the white ceramic giant pillar amidst the inaudible light sound of \"pu\", then dissolved in the flowing universe source essence.\n\nTo make the texture of the universe source essence better, Huatian continued to stir the slightly sticky black liquid in the cup at a constant speed, and the movements in her hands became comfortable as she got better at it, even half-narrowing her eyes and humming a cheerful tune.\n\nBut, for the tiny people in the universe, what kind of scene is it?\n\nFirst of all, what needs to be clear is that under the size difference huge enough to almost cross dimensions, it is absolutely impossible for tiny microorganisms to observe the great Little Huatian. The limit of what they can observe is just the thick universe barrier being instantly shattered by a white world moving at hundreds of millions of times the speed of light, then uncontrollably breaking into the universe and barbarically performing indescribable high-speed movements. Whether it is a nebula cluster or a super nebula cluster, in front of this white world, they are so tiny that they are far from being dust. As long as they are hit, they are instantly destroyed. Most living beings don't even know what happened to the universe until they die. And those lucky civilizations that were not directly involved can only get the absurd result of infinite extension up and down after using all scientific achievements for detection. After all, who could have thought that this exaggerated 