-  #  收到命令后，希瞳不耐烦地咋了一下舌。她手中正把玩着的一颗土著星球，被她像丢垃圾一样随手甩向了深空——那颗倒霉的星球在飞行过程中撞上了一片小行星带，瞬间炸成了一朵绚烂的烟花，但希瞳连看都懒得看一眼。\n“真麻烦……明明刚找到一点感觉。”\n虽然嘴上抱怨，但作为帝国舰娘的服从性还是让她动了起来。空间折跃的光芒一闪，下一秒，希瞳的身影便出现在了边境星域。\n当她看到远处那个粉色的巨大身影时，金色的瞳孔微微收缩了一下。（没有帝国识别码，没有能量回路反应……只是一个体积大一点的野生生物吗？）\n“作为野生巨娘来说，长得倒是不错。正好抓回去当个宠物。”\n希瞳冷笑一声，甚至没有完全展开战斗姿态。希瞳漫不经心地抬起手，掌心瞬间凝聚起数枚幽蓝色的反物质能量弹。这可是足以瞬间蒸发一支联合舰队的火力，她觉得用来打“招呼”已经足够给面子了。\n能量弹拖着长长的尾焰，精准地轰向了林凤的面门。 然而，预想中的爆炸和惨叫并没有出现。希瞳愣住了。 那几枚足以贯穿地壳的能量弹，在距离林凤鼻尖还有几千公里的地方，像是撞上了一堵看不见的墙壁连涟漪都没有泛起，就这样无声息地……消失了。\n林凤那双一直半眯着的紫色眼眸，缓缓睁开了一条缝。她甚至没有改变原本慵懒漂浮的姿势，只是微微侧过头，看向了这边飘在空中的希瞳。\n“哎呀……没想到呢。”\n“小人的文明也会豢养比他们还要强大不知道多少倍的存在么？“明明拥有能够将星间万物都当做玩物的身躯，却依旧自甘堕落戴上项圈充当虫子的看家犬……可真是委屈你了呢。”“但既然你已经攻击我了，可就别怪我还手咯～”\n林凤嘴角的笑意加深了，那是猎人看着落入陷阱的猎物时特有的温柔。\n希瞳还没来得及反驳，就看到林凤轻轻抬起了一根手指，只是简单的指尖轻点。刹那间，原本漆黑冰冷的宇宙真空，被染成了赤红色。 火球。 最基础的、毫无花哨的火球，但是是那种数量完全无法计算。\n“这种东西——！” 希瞳下意识地撑起护盾，试图嘲笑这种原始的攻击手段。但下一秒，她的脸色变了。 第一颗火球撞上护盾时，她感觉像被一颗恒星正面撞击。 紧接着是第二颗、第三颗、第一万颗……希瞳s vision 瞬间被无尽的烈焰吞没。她引以为傲的绝对防御在这一波火球术面前，脆弱得像是一层保鲜膜，仅仅坚持了不到三秒就宣告破碎。\n不知过了多久，攻击的频率慢慢降了下来。她在刻意控制节奏——就像是把猎物玩弄到半死之后的悠闲。林凤一边漫不经心地用几颗巨型火球将希瞳死死压制在原地，一边优雅地飘近，居高临下地看着狼狈不堪的希瞳。\n“虽然说我并不介意让你给这些小虫子们陪葬，但我还是挺乐意饶你一命的。毕竟，同类很难得嘛～”\n林凤伸出巨大的手指，轻轻挑起希瞳那已经满是灰尘和伤痕的下巴，强迫她抬起头。\n“只要你愿意求饶～怎么样？很划算的交易吧？”\n希瞳剧烈地喘息着，金色的竖瞳因为剧痛和屈辱而颤抖，但依然死死地盯着眼前这个恐怖的狐娘。\n“哈？……我对这些虫子们自我介绍的时候……你没听见么？咳咳……” 希瞳咬着牙，嘴角溢出一丝鲜血，试图维持最后的尊严，“我可是……御月家的希瞳……”\n“啧啧……看来还没听懂呢。”\n林凤遗憾地摇了摇头，手指微微用力，指尖燃起一缕更加纯粹的金色火焰，以此作为警告。\n“那就重新自我介绍一下吧——”\n在这无尽的星空背景下，林凤的声音如同宣判命运的神谕：\n“林凤。来自异界的旅者。” “以及——你往后余生都要用你的生命、用你的一切去侍奉的……主人。”
-  gts_linfeng.222.desc: "After receiving the order, Hitomi clicked her tongue impatiently. An aboriginal planet she was playing with in her hand was casually tossed into deep space like trash—the unlucky planet struck an asteroid belt in flight and instantly exploded into a brilliant firework, but Hitomi didn't even bother to glance back.\\n\"How troublesome... I was just starting to get a feel for it.\"\\nAlthough complaining, her obedience as an Imperial Shipgirl made her move. A flash of light from space fold, and the next second, Hitomi's figure appeared in the border star region.\\nWhen she saw that giant pink figure in the distance, her golden pupils contracted slightly. (No Imperial ID, no energy circuit reaction... is it just a slightly larger wild creature?)\\n\"For a wild Giantess, she looks quite good. I'll just catch her and keep her as a pet.\"\\nHitomi sneered, not even fully unfolding her combat stance. Hitomi casually lifted her hand, and several blue-colored antimatter energy balls instantly condensed in her palm. This was enough firepower to instantly vaporize a joint fleet; she felt it was enough to give \"face\" to use it as a \"greeting.\"\\nEnergy balls trailed long flame tails, accurately booming toward Linfeng's face. However, the expected explosion and screams did not appear. Hitomi was stunned. Those few energy balls, enough to pierce through a planetary crust, seemed to have hit an invisible wall thousands of kilometers away from Linfeng's nose without even causing a ripple, and vanished... just like that.\\nLinfeng's purple eyes, which had been half-squinted, slowly opened a crack. She didn't even change her originally lazy floating posture, merely tilted her head slightly and looked at Hitomi floating in the air.\\n\"Oh my... I didn't expect it.\"\\n\"Does the tiny people's civilization also keep beings who are countless times more powerful than them?\"\\n\"Clearly possessing a body that could treat everything in the stars as playthings, yet still willing to degenerate and wear a collar to serve as a watchdog for insects... it must be quite humiliating for you.\"\\n\"But since you've already attacked me, don't blame me for fighting back~\"\\nThe smile at the corner of Linfeng's mouth deepened; it was the specific tenderness of a hunter looking at prey that had fallen into a trap.\\nBefore Hitomi could refute, she saw Linfeng gently lift a finger, merely a simple tap of the fingertip. In an instant, the originally black and cold space vacuum was dyed a startling crimson. Fireballs. The most basic, unadorned fireballs, but in a number completely beyond calculation.\\n\"This kind of thing—!\" Hitomi subconsciously propped up a shield, attempting to mock such a primitive attack. But the next second, her expression changed. When the first fireball hit the shield, she felt as if she had been hit head-on by a star. \\nImmediately following were the second, third, ten-thousandth... Hitomi's vision was instantly engulfed by endless flames. Her proud absolute defense was as fragile as a piece of cling wrap before this wave of fireball magic, lasting less than three seconds before shattering.\\nAfter an unknown amount of time, the frequency of the attacks slowly slowed down. She was deliberately controlling the rhythm—like the leisure of playing with prey until it's half-dead. While carelessly suppressing Hitomi in place with several giant fireballs, Linfeng elegantly floated closer, looking down from above at the battered Hitomi.\\n\"Although I don't mind letting you be buried with these little insects, I'm still quite willing to spare your life. After all, it's rare to find one of the same kind~\"\\nLinfeng extended a giant finger, gently lifting Hitomi's chin, which was already full of dust and scars, forcing her to look up.\\n\"As long as you're willing to beg for mercy~ how about it? It's a very fair deal, isn't it?\"\\nHitomi breathed heavily, her golden slit pupils trembling from pain and humiliation, but still staring deathly at the terrifying fox girl before her.\\n\"Huh?... When I introduced myself
-    to these insects... didn't you hear me? *cough cough*...\" Hitomi gritted her teeth, a trace of blood overflowing from the corner of her mouth, attempting to maintain her last dignity, \"I am... Hitomi of the Otsuki Clan...\"\\n\"Tsk tsk... it seems you still haven't understood.\"\\nLinfeng shook her head regretfully, her finger applying slight pressure, a wisp of even purer golden flame igniting at the fingertip as a warning.\\n\"Then allow me to re-introduce myself—\"\\nAgainst this background of endless stars, Linfeng's voice sounded like a divine oracle pronouncing fate:\\n\"Linfeng. A traveler from another world.\"\\n\"And—the Master you will spend the rest of your life, with your existence, with your everything, to serve.\""
