   gts_seele.75.name: "Sea Gathering"
-  gts_seele.75.desc: "§B［Seele］§! returned to the Quantum Sea once more, whether to find a way back to her original world or simply to revisit past memories. When §B［Seele］§!’s enormous body appeared in the Quantum Sea, it undoubtedly shattered the peace that once existed there.\n\n‘Has nothing changed here?’ §B［Seele］§!’s azure eyes scanned her surroundings, her giantess-level perception allowing her to see everything clearly. After brushing away a few approaching quantum creatures, §B［Seele］§! prepared to venture deeper into the Quantum Sea...\n\nCountless world bubbles floated in the endless blue ocean, constantly forming and shattering, returning to the sea. The materials within them also exchanged, but the civilizations within had been destroyed by catastrophe, leaving only ruins to tell of past glories. §B［Seele］§!’s soft foot descended into the sea, the remnants of civilizations crushed into dust under the immense pressure. Even intact world bubbles couldn’t withstand the pressure and shattered under her feet, their contained galaxies attracted by the gravity of her foot, clinging to her skin like liquid, forming tiny stars. Stars that hadn’t been extinguished by her sweat continued to burn, but their energy couldn’t warm §B［Seele］§! in the slightest. Even the light from a supernova seemed insignificant on her vast foot.\n\nThe calm energy rippled due to the disturbance. ‘That feels ticklish, did §B［Seele］§! step on something?’ Feeling the strange sensation under her foot, §B［Seele］§! looked down, but there was nothing beneath her except the blue sea. Her azure eyes showed curiosity and confusion. ‘Probably... nothing important...’ Although the quantum creatures attacked §B［Seele］§!, their energy was absorbed the moment they touched her skin, having no effect. Meanwhile, they were torn apart by the energy generated by §B［Seele］§!’s movement, merging with the Quantum Sea.\n\nShould we follow §B［Seele］§! deeper into the Quantum Sea? Or just collect resources h