rface of the planet with her fingertip, feeling the minute protrusions on this small celestial body. Those cities and mountains that were once praised as their civilization's prides were now nothing more than small and indistinct dots between her fingerprints. Without further destruction, without any additional movements, she simply held the planet in her palm, turned around and walked towards the deep space. Through increasingly damaged sensors, the people on the planet could only watch their world being taken into the distance by white fingertips, and disappear at the end of the galaxy."
