   gts_xinuo.101.desc: "To avoid damage to the experimental facilities below, the archaeological team chose manual excavation. But excavating 1400 meters of soil layer takes too long. Finally, after discussion, the team decided to excavate 1100 meters with a stratum crusher, and explore the last 300 meters with a single-person excavation system, which can also help us precisely control the excavation area.\n\nThe stratum crusher was wrapped in a drop pod and fell from the science ship. Blazing fire enveloped its shell. One second... two seconds, then it smashed heavily underground. The foam inside cushioned the landing impact. The assembled stratum crusher made a rumbling sound. The ground within a fifty-meter radius began to shake violently. Web-like cracks appeared on the earth. The supposedly solid soil layer became soft in the constant vibration, then crushed into powder by the huge disc on the robotic arm. In just a minute, a big pit appeared on the ground. The machine roared continuously, the surface continued to sink, and layers of stairs were formed during the crushing. New sensors and molds allowed the machine to complete surface crushing and stair generation simultaneously, saving a lot of trouble. A few minutes later, a deep passage was revealed in front of everyone, and the machine's roar became smaller and smaller. The archaeological team put on equipment and went down along the stairs.\n\nThe pulse from the sonic probe scanned the surrounding environment. There was indeed only a layer of soil above, without any defense. But how it shield our science ship's detection equipment is intriguing. After the team walked down for a distance, the stratum shaking disappeared, presumably the crusher finished its task and stopped. The archaeological team accelerated their pace. Fifteen minutes later, they saw the green light of the crusher monitor below. After setting the return task, it slowly went up along the passage it came from, while the research team began manual exploration.\n\nAnother hour passed. The researchers finally reached the target depth. A solid metal ceiling appeared under our feet. This might be the institute's fortification. Relying on the sonic probe, the archaeological team found multiple paths, each seemingly leading to a major city of this planet. But the priority is to find a place to enter and exit the facility. After digging further to one side, a spacious underground cave appeared in front of the archaeological team. The place where the institute is located is only a small part of this underground cave. Using laser ranging, the diameter of this cave reached 420 kilometers. In such a space, whether highways or production facilities, they were arranged on a solid platform. Buildings were uniformly painted white, seemingly to improve visibility in the dark underground environment. Street lamps stood like loyal guards on both sides of the street, still standing upright even though the entire underground facility was abandoned."
   # 部署软梯后，考古团队沿着墙壁下去，手电的光线刺入黑暗的心脏，驱散了地下的阴霾。沿着白色的走廊向前，一道高耸的钢铁大门出现在了我们的眼前，似乎是因为失去电力的缘故，厚重的大门虚掩着，考古团队正好可以借此进入研究院。\n\n室内杂乱不堪，手电光照射的地方全是散落的纸片，队员们收集着纸片，拼凑着数据，一个针对星神兽的基因计划浮出了水面，早已消失的帝国竟然通过提取星神兽的基因来制造生物兵器，但现有的数据大多都是废弃的，考古团队必须继续深入，寻找更多有效信息，希望一切顺利。\n\n考古团队摸索着前进，虽然这里并没有交火的痕迹，但许多东西早已被人为破坏，甚至还有焚烧的痕迹，不知是否是紧急销毁实验数据，失落的帝国到底被什么入侵，以至于他们如此恐惧？在建筑中不断搜索着，考古团队并没有什么发现，但启动的声波探测装置却在一面光滑的墙后找到了一条通往更深地区的隧道。这种桥段真像古代小说里的剧情，或许我们应该进去看看？
   gts_xinuo.102.desc: "After deploying the rope ladder, the archaeological team went down along the wall. Flashlight beams pierced the heart of darkness, dispelling the underground haze. Moving forward along the white corridor, a towering steel gate appeared in front of us. It seemed that due to power loss, the heavy gate was left ajar, just right for the archaeological team to enter the institute.\n\nThe room was messy. Places illuminated by flashlights were full of scattered papers. The team members collected papers and pieced together data. A gene plan targeting Star Gods surfaced. The long-gone empire actually created biological weapons by extracting Star God genes. But existing data was mostly scrapped. The archaeological team must go deeper to find more effective information. Ideally everything goes smoothly.\n\nThe archaeological team groped forward. Although there were no traces of crossfire here, many things had long been artificially destroyed, and there were even traces of burning. Unknown if it was emergency destruction of experimental data. What invaded the lost empire to make them so fearful? Searching constantly in the building, the archaeological team found nothing. But the activated sonic probe found a tunnel leading to a deeper area behind a smooth wall. This plot is really like an ancient novel. Maybe we should go in and have a look?"
-  # 压抑……黑暗的空间总是会让人感觉不舒服，即使有小队一起行动，也难以抵挡长时间的寂静，焦虑蔓延开来，到了地下室后，这样压抑的感觉更为浓烈，一股直击心灵的震慑不断在周围产生，巨大的压力让团队的进度异常缓慢，但越靠近地下室，这样的感觉就越轻，似乎地下室有着什么东西在抵抗着心灵冲击，团队迅速转移至地下室门口，不知道这么长久的时间过去了，什么东西还能保持着这样的光芒，不过我们无法打开这扇门，门禁系统依然在工作着，这样持久的能源或许也值得我们的科研团队去研究，但当务之急依然是寻找可以打开门禁的物品，这些东西应该就散落在大厅之中。\n\n团队返回大厅，从杂乱的物品中寻找着那一丝希望，在大厅上上下下都搜索过后，一个吊牌被找到，人像与其上的字早已模糊，不过卡片应该还能使用，在将卡片放上去后，门成功打开，实验室内被一层厚厚的玻璃所围绕，一条走廊围绕着这个房间，明亮的蓝光完全驱散了地下的阴霾与沉闷，但依然没人能看清那里藏着什么，黑色的隔离门将里面与外面分割为了两个世界，再次刷卡，广播中轻柔的女声传来：\n\n§Y“艾丝菲雅主管，欢迎回来。”§!\n\n卡片的主人在这一刻终于被揭露，但是我们没有在收集的资料中发现任何关于这个人的信息。\n\n沉重的铁门缓缓打开，一个一人多高的培养舱出现在了众人眼前，透明的玻璃罐中一个赤身裸体的少女正在沉睡，及腰的蓝发随其中的液体散，头上的两只角上镶嵌着三对淡黄色的宝石，更令人吃惊的是，少女背后有一对一人高的翅膀，翅膀向周围发射着明亮的蓝光将她包裹在其中，但这样的光亮并没有让人感到刺眼，反而用一种神奇的力量抚慰着所有人的身体，随后流入人们的精神之中，疲惫与不安一扫而空，取而代之的是一种悠闲的感觉，仿佛在此刻看到了蔚蓝的天空与碧绿的草原，但研究员们没有沉溺在这样的体验当中，他们依然在寻找着可能了解到罐中少女的身世，将收集到的信息总和后，一个复杂而庞大的计划被勾勒出来。
