-  gts_evt_random.040246.desc: "After the Giantesses arrived together, bringing laughter and wild, playful games, this game of destruction that had swept through the entire Tiny Person Capital Area was far from over. As the second act of the game of destruction, Hitomi, Su Xiaobai, and Linfeng bid a temporary farewell to Niao Yin and the others, carving out a brand-new “playground” exclusively for themselves in a neighboring city cluster. Under the azure sky, three slender figures, each towering thousands of meters high, descended slowly. Their summer swimsuits were still speckled with a trace of dust left over from the previous game, and a shadow large enough to block out the sun instantly engulfed the entire bustling coastal metropolis. Linfeng, who had been shoved to the very front, was still in a state of utter bewilderment; she rubbed her eyes in confusion:  n\n§U Huh? Are we… here already?§!\n\nBefore she could fully come to her senses, three pairs of flawless, fair, bare feet had already touched the ground. Boom—! Amid violent tremors, the sea water surged into a tsunami hundreds of meters high. The golden sandy beach—along with the tens of thousands of terrified, screaming Tiny persons on it—was mercilessly crushed by the giant foot into the deepest depths of the earth in an instant, reduced to tiny red specks stuck to the Giantess’s soles. Hitomi narrowed her eyes slightly, gazing contentedly at the magnificent ocean vista before her, and sighed with satisfaction: §Y, this is so wonderful—§! Meanwhile, her heel was casually grinding—like a cat sharpening its claws—across a luxury resort villa complex, mercilessly reducing it to an unrecognizable mixture of blood and rebar. \n\nAt that moment, Su Xiaobai, standing in the center, extended her slender finger and tapped a flickering holographic panel into existence in midair. \n\n§M “The rules of this game are very simple: the higher the destruction level and the more impressive your KD (kill-death ratio), the more generous the rewards you can redeem.”§!\n\nUpon reading these rules, the proactive Hitomi and Xiaobai exchanged a glance, both curling the corners of their mouths into mischievous grins. They immediately flanked the unsuspecting Linfeng, one in front and one behind. Forcibly pushed toward the city center by her two mischievous companions, Linfeng frantically waved her arms while shouting, “No, please don’t!” However, once Linfeng’s competitive spirit was ignited, she, too, became incredibly eager. Lifting her soft, massive feet, she stomped heavily toward the densest cluster of skyscrapers in the city center. At that moment, inside those skyscrapers—towering hundreds of meters high—countless tiny humans were plunged into utter despair. Through the shattering glass facades, they could only watch in terror as a pale pink sole—so vast it blocked out the sky—slowly closed in, radiating an overwhelming aura of power. Countless tiny persons scrambled frantically like headless flies within the confined spaces, trampling one another as their screams merged into a single, deafening chorus. Linfeng merely applied a tiny bit more force, gently pressing down with the arch of her foot, and the entire sturdy Financial Center tower crumbled and exploded beneath her delicate sole as fragilely as a sandcastle on the beach, turning into a cloud of dust. \n\nSeeing Linfeng having such a good time, Su Xiaobai sighed with a touch of resignation, but for the sake of the reward she was determined to claim, she, too, began to stroll elegantly through the city. Her massive, sky-obscuring pink fox tails swept wildly through the air; with every swing, they wiped out entire residential districts as if they were mere rags. Hitomi stood there, tilting her head slightly, silently gazing down at the chaotic, devastating scene below that resembled an anthill. Her enormous bare feet—large enough to block out the sky—were in no hurry to trample everything in sight. Instead, as if plotting some mischievous prank, they hovered leisurely above the super bridge spanning the bay. She deliberately wiggled her fair, delicate toes lightly above the bridge, casting a massive shadow that flickered on and off across the deck, wantonly toying with the hundreds of cars—now linked together like a fiery dragon—as they fled in a frantic panic. As she watched the tiny persons on the bridge sink into hysterical panic and despair at the sight of this inescapable giant foot, the mischievous grin on Hitomi’s lips grew wider. Finally, just as the terrified screams of the tiny persons reached their peak, she seemed to casually step down. With a thunderous “BOOM,” that delicate, perfect giant foot snapped the entire magnificent superbridge in two. Under the immense pressure, countless vehicles on the bridge deck were mercilessly crushed into thin metal discs. Hitomi even gleefully twisted her ankle slightly, maliciously grinding her delicate heel against the broken bridge pier a few times, letting those desperate wails be mercilessly crushed and, along with the alloy debris, lightly kicked into the churning waves."
