-  gts_evt_random.040249.desc: "After a period of revelry, the girls—who had been scattered in small groups, each toying with their Tiny people—converged on the metropolitan area of the capital city where they had first arrived. The six of them sat in a circle atop the Deep Space Broadcasting Array, now reduced to near ruins, sharing amusing anecdotes from their earlier adventures, their voices full of relaxation and contentment. The girls, who were praising this miniature civilization from every angle, paid no attention whatsoever to the tiny people nestled in the cracks of the ruins beneath their seats or those at their feet, worshipfully licking the skin of their legs. \n\nThey chatted animatedly about their plans for their next visit, mapping out a journey to explore every valley, beach, and lake on this planet—yet for the Tiny persons, every arrival and every playful frolic by the Giantesses brought with it a catastrophe of epic proportions. \n\nNight slowly enveloped the shattered capital. The girls took over the entire city, sleeping on the ground around the relatively intact landmarks by the light of broken and dimmed lamps. Their massive bodies pressed down on the remaining structures, causing the few intact buildings to continue crumbling. Occasionally, their skin would sense a faint rustling sound, and the girls couldn’t help but chuckle inwardly, reveling in their sense of superiority over the tiny people. \n\nThe tiny people, trembling nervously amid the ruins, listened to the steady breathing of the six girls above them, their hearts filled with nothing but endless desolation. \n\nThose who first set foot among the Stars had once believed that tolerance and goodwill could unite all life in the Milky Way, yet they overlooked the unbridgeable chasm between size, perception, and approaches to survival. A single, unreserved vacation promotion had reduced an entire civilization to a sandbox toy for six Giantesses to relieve their stress."
