 something was off with their god. Panic spread immediately as everyone knelt down, anxiously praising the greatness of their god, afraid that she would withdraw her divine grace.\n\nYaorong looked at the starbase. The giant base that her father called \"Citadel\" could now fit easily between her teeth. And the largest colony ships that those little guys had were at most comparable to the ion cannons on a fortress.\n\nSuch tiny colony ships wanted to explore her body......\n\n\"Compatriots! The time has come for His Majesty and God to test us! For the sake of God's safety, how can we forsake our duties?\"\n\nThe voice of a little guy was quite impassioned, it would seem that the guy was the leader among them. But the statement he made put a sense of helplessness in Yaorong  -  what does it mean \"for the sake of God's safety\" ? What danger could she possibly be in? Even the Stars were nothing more than a snack to her.\n\nEven so, Yaorong had no intention of speaking out against his statement. Watching them make a ruckus was a lot of fun. At least, when she was not spending time with her sister looking for sources of fun (and food), or teasing her father, these followers who viewed her as their mother were a source of amusement to her."
