-  gts_god_keeper.5603.desc: "As always, Ivan lay in this vast crimson world that was beyond his capacity to explore in his life. It was the body of their most revered, most respected God. A single wrinkle in her belly was enormous enough to build multiple districts in.\n\n“Indeed worthy of our God…”\n\nAt the very same moment that Ivan sighed, a dreadful humming echoed, but to him and the other parasites housed inside Yaorong’s belly, this terrifying sound did not mean a disaster-rather the opposite. The sound was a sign that their God was simply starting to eat.\n\nAnd their God beginning to eat also meant that their resources for the next few months or even years would be secured. While picking up the remains that have been almost, completely, digested from the folds inside God was indeed an option, nothing beat snatching the food from the God’s mouth-assisting the God’s digestion was one of their missions, after all!\n\nThe crimson world began to shake. Soon after, pieces of planets of unimaginable sizes began to fall from the cardia, but inside Yaorong’s liquids they merely rippled. Of course, this was when compared to Yaorong’s entire stomach. In Ivan’s perspective, the waves produced by the falling planet fragments were one of the most magnificent sceneries he had ever laid eyes upon.\n\n“Compatriots! It’s time to gather resources!”\n\nIvan, as a scout, sent out the message. But this time, the commotion was so overwhelming, that even those in charge of collecting resources who did not get the message would have arrived quickly. For him, for now, all he had to do was marvel at this “beauty”.\n\nWith the specialized equipment, Ivan saw the planet fragments, or, rather, the continental shelves gradually dissolving in Yaorong’s gastric fluids. He wasn't very clear about it. Though he had seen this not just once, he didn't dare ask his God what kind of strange things she ate--was it reasonable for him to pat the crimson surface and ask whether his God had eaten yet?. \n\n“A relatively complete city was found with standard industrial districts… Did God eat a planet from the enemy?”\n\nSwallowing an entire planet may seem like a terrifying gesture, but to a being whose internal body is capable of forming an independent ecology, and whose body can be larger than a star in times of need, a habitable planet was probably the same as a candy or a small bread.\n\nTheir empire had been in constant war. As the princess and guardian god of the empire, Yaorong was not only the most terrifying deterrent, but also the greatest weapon. Aside from the Fallen Empire’s main fleets, no fleet had ever stopped her pace. And on the topic of planets from opposing empires…\n\nLooking at the planet fragments bathing in the tumultuous gastric fluids, Ivan felt a tinge of pity for those people. Excluding the planetary defense forces, most of these people probably did not deserve to die. But there was no alternative. They had foolishly chosen to start a war with their empire, and therefore they deserved their fate.\n\nThere were three landing strategies for the Empire. The first one was to have super-heavy mobile fortresses lead the way, followed by mobile construction crews, and then powerful psionics gifted by God. The former ensured the stability of the advance, and the latter was in charge of the killing. This method had the least destruction. The second landing strategy involved Yaorong, or her sister, shrinking themself down and playing on the planet--usually at sizes ranging from 10 kilometers to 100 kilometers. The damage caused by the two princesses when they “played” was often second only to launching the Empire’s “Colossus” on the planet. \n\nAnd the third landing was the cruelest. The God, at her normal size, would directly devour the enemy planet. Or… Ivan had heard of a particularly cruel execution that their God had enacted. There was once a country called 'Dragon Is Very Strong, Poisonous Rock Man', which insulted their empire. Months after their war began, the God stepped foot into the same system used by her coworkers. \n\nAfter capturing
-    their guardian dragon, the capital was crushed under God’s toes, and even the remaining residue was licked clean by God’s younger sister. \n\nThis was the God they served and believed in. She showed her tenderness and strength to the citizens of the empire as much as she could. She showed her gentle and seductive side to her father, and showcased her terrifyingly arrogant and invincible power to the enemies of the empire.\n\nAt least… that was the situation now.\n\n............"
+  gts_god_keeper.5603.desc: "As always, Ivan lay in this vast crimson world that was beyond his capacity to explore in his life. It was the body of their most revered, most respected God. A single wrinkle in her belly was enormous enough to build multiple districts in.\n\n\"Indeed worthy of our God...\"\n\nAt the very same moment that Ivan sighed, a dreadful humming echoed, but to him and the other parasites housed inside Yaorong's belly, this terrifying sound did not mean a disaster-rather the opposite. The sound was a sign that their God was simply starting to eat.\n\nAnd their God beginning to eat also meant that their resources for the next few months or even years would be secured. While picking up the remains that have been almost, completely, digested from the folds inside God was indeed an option, nothing beat snatching the food from the God's mouth-assisting the God's digestion was one of their missions, after all!\n\nThe crimson world began to shake. Soon after, pieces of planets of unimaginable sizes began to fall from the cardia, but inside Yaorong's liquids they merely rippled. Of course, this was when compared to Yaorong's entire stomach. In Ivan's perspective, the waves produced by the falling planet fragments were one of the most magnificent sceneries he had ever laid eyes upon.\n\n\"Compatriots! It's time to gather resources!\"\n\nIvan, as a scout, sent out the message. But this time, the commotion was so overwhelming, that even those in charge of collecting resources who did not get the message would have arrived quickly. For him, for now, all he had to do was marvel at this \"beauty\".\n\nWith the specialized equipment, Ivan saw the planet fragments, or, rather, the continental shelves gradually dissolving in Yaorong's gastric fluids. He wasn't very clear about it. Though he had seen this not just once, he didn't dare ask his God what kind of strange things she ate--was it reasonable for him to pat the crimson surface and ask whether his God had eaten yet?. \n\n\"A relatively complete city was found with standard industrial districts... Did God eat a planet from the enemy?\"\n\nSwallowing an entire planet may seem like a terrifying gesture, but to a being whose internal body is capable of forming an independent ecology, and whose body can be larger than a star in times of need, a habitable planet was probably the same as a candy or a small bread.\n\nTheir empire had been in constant war. As the princess and guardian god of the empire, Yaorong was not only the most terrifying deterrent, but also the greatest weapon. Aside from the Fallen Empire's main fleets, no fleet had ever stopped her pace. And on the topic of planets from opposing empires...\n\nLooking at the planet fragments bathing in the tumultuous gastric fluids, Ivan felt a tinge of pity for those people. Excluding the planetary defense forces, most of these people probably did not deserve to die. But there was no alternative. They had foolishly chosen to start a war with their empire, and therefore they deserved their fate.\n\nThere were three landing strategies for the Empire. The first one was to have super-heavy mobile fortresses lead the way, followed by mobile construction crews, and then powerful psionics gifted by God. The former ensured the stability of the advance, and the latter was in charge of the killing. This method had the least destruction. The second landing strategy involved Yaorong, or her sister, shrinking themself down and playing on the planet--usually at sizes ranging from 10 kilometers to 100 kilometers. The damage caused by the two princesses when they \"played\" was often second only to launching the Empire's \"Colossus\" on the planet. \n\nAnd the third landing was the cruelest. The God, at her normal size, would directly devour the enemy planet. Or... Ivan had heard of a particularly cruel execution that their God had enacted. There was once a country called 'Dragon Is Very Strong, Poisonous Rock Man', which insulted their empire. Months after their war began, the God stepped foot into the same system used by her coworkers. \n\nAfter capturing
+    their guardian dragon, the capital was crushed under God's toes, and even the remaining residue was licked clean by God's younger sister. \n\nThis was the God they served and believed in. She showed her tenderness and strength to the citizens of the empire as much as she could. She showed her gentle and seductive side to her father, and showcased her terrifyingly arrogant and invincible power to the enemies of the empire.\n\nAt least... that was the situation now.\n\n............"
