s stars birthed  from its body. When the collective beliefs of mankind gather together, their expression of faith also becomes apparent: a real star god, a real god flying in the universe. \"§!\n\nThe governor spoke each and every word that was carved on the stone tablet that was erected in front of the silver white giant egg.  However, every time he said a word, his voice trembled a little more.\n\n§Y\"Even that star god, the god that was created by countless stars, the god who received the faith of all living beings in space was not invincible.\"§!\n\n\"Leader... that was the precursors and their god.\"\n\nCivilization is never the lonely vigil. Our clan's development was also inseparable from the full support from the precursors - from our language to the design concept of the FTL engine, we received help from the precursor civilizations whom we had never met.  But, aside from that Ideal City Ruins, which had been transformed into a statue for our God, they did not leave any traces on our planets!\n\nExcept for the little dragon, who didn't know much but was playing with her tail on the side, were joy and amazement filling everywhere in this rift.   It's not that the little dragon wasn't aware of what her father was talking about, but she simply didn't know what the precursors meant. In fact, if you had not put on an expression like \" If you move that egg again, you will stay in the corner to think about things\", the little dragon might have started eating the pure white giant egg, which had the same scale as her; after all, the little one rarely gets to see such \"normal food\". \n\n§Y \"Gods are not invincible, gods will bleed, gods will die.\"§!\n\n§Y \"We will defy the gods.\" §!"
